Date: Fri, 17 Jul 2026 15:16:30 -0400
Subject: [PATCH 07239/11362] [outer-loop] bp35 L9 round 24 (gpt-5.6-sol via
 codex): rung-gain candidates A-F bounded, honest null

Dispatched gpt-5.6-sol via codex CLI to test round 23's untested rung-gain
leads against bp35 L9. Result: all six candidates (against-gravity carry,
multi-column geometry, door-open timing, floor/toggle reachability, bottom
symmetry) bounded to honest nulls. Best surviving rest remains world -9.5;
no rest found in [-13,-48]; frontier unchanged at 8/9.

New mechanics found: ACTION7 is a cell-exact reversible door undo (restores
all 32 carved cells but regains no height); door-gap refill is impossible
under any tested timing (0 cells change on re-click); final-carry click
coordinates are hitbox-invariant over a 25-point sweep (always dy=-6);
against-gravity clicks never carry the player.

Independently verified before committing: reviewed the full artifact and
registry diff, ran scripts/adversarial_verify.py (0 flagged), spawned an
independent hostile-reviewer sub-agent (found solve_provenance claim
consistent with CLAUDE.md's adapter-free-explore-induce category, not a
mislabel as initially flagged -- verified against the taxonomy text
directly), recomputed the reproducibility checksum from the raw action
tail (matches exactly), and independently replayed the 20-action
diagnostic tail 3x from fresh envs myself (all 3: level 8, GAME_OVER,
deterministic -- matches the artifact's own claim).

Evidence: results/outer_loop_round24_bp35_probe_l9_20260717.json

Co-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
