 - 2026-07-17 [outer-loop]: bp35 L9 round 23 (claude-fable-5, operator: "try the disambiguation experiment for eye-kill vs above-view-kill") — RESOLVED decisively: the ascent kill is CROSSING THE STATIC VIEWPORT TOP mid-flight (screen row 0), not the -55 eye row (two-point proof: identical screen-row-0 deaths at world rows 0 and -48 under cameras 48 rows apart). Round 22's "camera hard-clamp at -48" is retracted — the camera recenters to rest−38.5 (up) / rest−28.5 (down) after each settle and never moves during flight; -48 was merely the camera at the highest rest achieved (-9.5). Flight-survival law: a float survives iff its landing rest lies within the current static viewport — this also mechanically explains round 16's grow-first-survives observation. The L9 seal is now quantified as a ~3-pixel shortfall: the first rest above the slab (~-51) needs a prior rest ≤ -12.5 vs best-achievable -9.5; one 6px rung (the door cell at -15.5) would cascade the whole tower open (toggle row + upper switches clickable). Rung-gain attempts all null this round; focused next leads recorded. No new level (frontier stays 8/9). Evidence: results/outer_loop_round23_bp35_probe_l9_20260717.json (adversarial-verify clean); registry gotcha appended.
+- 2026-07-17 [outer-loop]: bp35 L9 round 24 (gpt-5.6-sol) tested the requested missing-rung candidates through public-frame-only fresh-env probes: against-gravity clicks never carry upward; multi-column/remote-shelf geometries block, crush, or converge to the same -9.5 rest; all 25 final-carry click offsets produced identical dy=-6; safe DOWN door carve followed by UP still dies at the active view top, and the carved gap cannot be refilled (0 changed cells). ACTION7 cell-exactly restores the 32-cell door carve but gains no height. The -51 floor/toggle row remain unreachable, and only +12 downward drops were found, so bottom-edge symmetry remains inconclusive. Three diagnostic endpoints replayed byte-identically 3/3 each; no new level, frontier stays 8/9. Evidence: results/outer_loop_round24_bp35_probe_l9_20260717.json (adversarial-verify clean).
